{"name":"Kilauea Lava","hex":"#843d38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lava","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The molten rock ejected by a volcano from a vent such as a crater or fissure; magma that has breached the surface of the earth.","A body of lava."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lava"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kīlauea","blocks":[{"text":"Kīlauea is an active shield volcano in the Hawaiian Islands, located along the southeastern shore of Hawaii Island. The volcano is between 210,000 and 280,000 years old and grew above sea level about 100,000 years ago. Since the islands were settled, it has been the most active of the five volcanoes that together form the island and among the most active volcanoes on Earth. The most recent eruption of Kīlauea began in December 2024 inside Halemaʻumaʻu, a pit crater located within Kīlauea's summit caldera, with episodic lava fountains and flows currently continuing inside the crater into late 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Episode_4_of_Kilauea%27s_December_2024_eruption_2025-01-16.jpg/330px-Episode_4_of_Kilauea%27s_December_2024_eruption_2025-01-16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C4%ABlauea","wikidata":"Q188698"},{"title":"Lava","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is magma that has been expelled from the interior of a terrestrial planet or a moon onto its surface. Lava may be erupted at a volcano or through a fracture in the crust, on land or underwater, usually at temperatures from 800 to 1,200 °C. Lava may be erupted directly onto the land surface or onto the sea floor or it may be ejected into the atmosphere before falling back down. The solid volcanic rock resulting from subsequent cooling of the molten material is often also called lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava","wikidata":"Q40157"},{"title":"Lava (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is a color that is a purplish shade of red. It is named after the color of volcanic lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Pahoeoe_fountain_edit2.jpg/330px-Pahoeoe_fountain_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_(color)","wikidata":"Q6502169"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg/500px-Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg/1280px-Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg/500px-Kilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKilauea_-_Landsat_mosaic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Kilauea_ali_2012_01_28.jpg/500px-Kilauea_ali_2012_01_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Kilauea_ali_2012_01_28.jpg/500px-Kilauea_ali_2012_01_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKilauea_ali_2012_01_28.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Rainbow_and_eruption_of_Halema%60uma%60u_vent_at_Kilauea.jpg/500px-Rainbow_and_erup